{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"id":"EarendilWorks.pi","latestVersion":"1.5.2","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"author":"Mario Zechner","copyright":"Copyright (c) 2026 Mario Zechner","description":"AI coding assistant with read, bash, edit, write tools","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"author":"Mario Zechner","copyright":"Copyright (c) 2026 Mario Zechner","description":"AI coding assistant with read, bash, edit, write tools","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"Pi is a minimal terminal coding harness. Adapt pi to your workflows, not the other way around, without having to fork and modify pi internals. Extend it with TypeScript Extensions, Skills, Prompt Templates, and Themes. Put your extensions, skills, prompt templates, and themes in Pi Packages and share them with others via npm or git.\nPi ships with powerful defaults but skips features like sub agents and plan mode. Instead, you can ask pi to build what you want or install a third party pi package that matches your workflow.\nPi runs in four modes: interactive, print or JSON, RPC for process integration, and an SDK for embedding in your own apps. See openclaw/openclaw for a real-world SDK integration.","moniker":"pi","name":"pi","packageUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi","publisher":"EARENDIL INC.","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works","releaseNotes":"New Features\n- Fork sessions whose folder is gone: when a session's original folder was moved or deleted, you can now fork it into the current folder instead of only continuing, so later resumes no longer ask. See Continue or switch sessions.\nChanged\n- When a session's working directory no longer exists, for example after the project folder was renamed, interactive mode now offers Continue, Fork, or Cancel instead of only continuing. Continue runs the session in the current directory without storing the choice, as before; Fork copies it into the current directory as a new session with a new ID, like --fork, so the next resume no longer asks. This applies at startup (--session, --resume), to /resume, to /import, and to ctx.switchSession() from extensions (#11975 by @petrroll, fixes #11060)\nFixed\n- Fixed /import of a session whose working directory no longer exists leaving a copy in the session directory, and continuing it leaving a second copy with the same ID (s.jsonl and s-1.jsonl); the failed copy is now removed (#11975 by @petrroll, fixes #11060)\n- Fixed Anthropic OAuth requests reporting an outdated Claude Code version","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/releases/tag/v1.5.2","tags":["agent","agentic","ai","chatbot","code","coding","large-language-model","llm","programming"]},"zh-CN":{"description":"具备读取、Bash、编辑、写入工具的 AI 编程助手","locale":"zh-CN","longDescription":"Pi 是一款轻量型终端编码工具集。无需复刻并修改 Pi 的内部代码，就能让 Pi 适配你的工作流，而非反过来让你迁就 Pi。你可以通过 TypeScript 扩展、技能模块、提示词模板和主题对 Pi 进行拓展。把你开发的扩展、技能模块、提示词模板和主题打包为 Pi 包，即可通过 npm 或 git 分享给其他用户。\nPi 默认搭载的功能十分强大，但未内置子代理、计划模式这类功能。你可以让 Pi 生成你需要的功能，或是安装适配你工作流的第三方 Pi 包即可。\nPi 支持四种运行模式：交互模式、打印/JSON 输出模式、用于流程集成的 RPC 模式，以及可嵌入你自有应用的 SDK 模式。实际的 SDK 集成案例可参考 openclaw/openclaw 项目。","tags":["人工智能","代码","大语言模型","智能体","编程","聊天机器人","自主智能"]}},"longDescription":"Pi is a minimal terminal coding harness. Adapt pi to your workflows, not the other way around, without having to fork and modify pi internals. Extend it with TypeScript Extensions, Skills, Prompt Templates, and Themes. Put your extensions, skills, prompt templates, and themes in Pi Packages and share them with others via npm or git.\nPi ships with powerful defaults but skips features like sub agents and plan mode. Instead, you can ask pi to build what you want or install a third party pi package that matches your workflow.\nPi runs in four modes: interactive, print or JSON, RPC for process integration, and an SDK for embedding in your own apps. See openclaw/openclaw for a real-world SDK integration.","moniker":"pi","name":"pi","packageUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi","publisher":"EARENDIL INC.","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works","releaseNotes":"New Features\n- Fork sessions whose folder is gone: when a session's original folder was moved or deleted, you can now fork it into the current folder instead of only continuing, so later resumes no longer ask. See Continue or switch sessions.\nChanged\n- When a session's working directory no longer exists, for example after the project folder was renamed, interactive mode now offers Continue, Fork, or Cancel instead of only continuing. Continue runs the session in the current directory without storing the choice, as before; Fork copies it into the current directory as a new session with a new ID, like --fork, so the next resume no longer asks. This applies at startup (--session, --resume), to /resume, to /import, and to ctx.switchSession() from extensions (#11975 by @petrroll, fixes #11060)\nFixed\n- Fixed /import of a session whose working directory no longer exists leaving a copy in the session directory, and continuing it leaving a second copy with the same ID (s.jsonl and s-1.jsonl); the failed copy is now removed (#11975 by @petrroll, fixes #11060)\n- Fixed Anthropic OAuth requests reporting an outdated Claude Code version","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/releases/tag/v1.5.2","tags":["agent","agentic","ai","chatbot","code","coding","large-language-model","llm","programming"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.5.2/app.json","detailSha256":"701fdf75f63a85faf06500ef2366f1338c37968b837a01b34fb27de91877ad03","releaseDate":"2026-11-10","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"1.5.2"